---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import RtlContinuity from "../components/RtlContinuity.astro";
import SnapshotTiming from "../components/SnapshotTiming.astro";
import BrowserSession from "../components/BrowserSession.astro";
import { evidenceUrl, evidenceAsset, url } from "../lib/specs";
import capture from "../../../docs/evidence/rtl-continuity/capture.json";
const rows = [
 ["Direct coverage", "Manufacturer: approximately 500 kHz–1.766 GHz, including the HF upconverter. Full coverage and sensitivity are not locally characterized.", "Start with normal 2.4 GHz. Upstream reports experimental wider tuning; accepted commands do not prove RF coverage."],
 ["Sample format", "Normal USB IQ is 8-bit I + 8-bit Q. Four internal-pattern transport rates were measured; a separate 5-second normal-IQ file was captured.", "Upstream advertises 16/40/80 MS/s snapshots, 8/10-bit output and at most 16,380 pairs. 600/600 CRC/count passes across all six nominal rate/format combinations; known-signal RF response is unverified."],
 ["Continuity", "Four 65-second test-mode trials: no reported gap at 1.024/2.4/2.56 MS/s; ≥80 missing bytes at 2.048 MS/s. This does not prove RF-mode continuity or absolute zero loss.", "Upstream maximum windows calculate to 1.024/0.410/0.205 ms at 16/40/80 MS/s. Measured median command-to-payload ≈361 ms (8-bit) /451 ms (10-bit). At 80 MS/s nominal series time coverage is 0.0565% / 0.0451%, not event hit probability."],
 ["Instantaneous spectrum", "A few MHz per tuning. The FM-band survey hops sequentially; it is not a simultaneous 20 MHz capture.", "Tens of MHz in a nominal snapshot, subject to filtering and actual RF behavior. Calibrated usable bandwidth remains open."],
 ["Front end", "Manufacturer specifies SMA, filtering and 1 ppm TCXO. Actual antenna/source identity, frequency error and sensitivity were not verified.", "Wi-Fi RF path and carrier antenna need physical characterization. Ten-bit output does not prove better dynamic range than RTL eight-bit output."],
 ["Current hardware result", "V4/R828D identified; transport trial complete; ambient FM candidate has reproducible 19 kHz structure. Station, antenna and decoder result remain unverified.", "Original ESP32/4 MiB identified; original bytes preserved/restored. Clean 921,600-baud firmware answers complete queries and delivers full-size snapshots. RF clocks, tuning response and known signals remain unverified."],
 ["Transmit", "Receive-only in this normal SDR configuration.", "ESP-SDR implements RX. Ordinary Wi-Fi TX is separate from arbitrary waveform SDR transmission."]
];
const applications = [
 ["FM receiver development", "V4", "Measured normal-IQ candidate and FM-like pilot structure. Verify antenna/station and audio or decoder output before calling the selected application complete."],
 ["Long HF/VHF/UHF recordings", "V4", "Manufacturer-supported bands and continuous USB architecture; antenna, RF-mode continuity and application performance need targeted tests."],
 ["ADS-B, AIS, airband, 433 MHz sensors", "V4", "Suitable direct bands and established host tools; none of these applications was demonstrated in this evaluation."],
 ["Wide 2.4 GHz observation", "ESP32 candidate", "Upstream-supported snapshot path; local CRC/count integrity and nominal time coverage are measured, while controlled RF response is pending."],
 ["Repeatable short bursts / BLE", "ESP32 experiment", "Bounded source/decoder tools exist. Counted emissions, capture hit rate and verified payload remain physical gates."],
 ["FPGA-assisted processing", "Separate research route", "Reviewed bounded snapshot/SPI architecture and capacity budgets. No FPGA transport, DMA or integrated RF benchmark yet."]
];
---
<Base title="Two receivers, measured progress">
<header class="page-title"><p class="eyebrow">RTL-SDR BLOG V4 / ORIGINAL ESP32</p><h1>Keep both receivers.<br />Measure their different jobs.</h1><p class="lede">The V4 already delivers normal IQ and measured continuous test data. The ESP32 now delivers CRC-checked snapshots with measured transfer gaps; controlled signal behavior remains unverified. Their useful stock bands serve different applications.</p><p><a href={evidenceUrl("docs/evidence/rtl-continuity/README.md")}>RTL transport evidence</a> · <a href={evidenceUrl("docs/evidence/rtl-fm-survey/README.md")}>Measured FM candidate</a> · <a href={evidenceUrl("docs/evidence/sdr-diagnostic-trial/README.md")}>ESP command-loop diagnostic</a></p></header>
<div class="table-scroll"><table class="lab-table"><thead><tr><th>Question</th><th>Attached RTL-SDR Blog V4</th><th>Attached ESP32 / ESP-SDR trial</th></tr></thead><tbody>{rows.map(row => <tr>{row.map((cell,i) => i === 0 ? <th scope="row">{cell}</th> : <td>{cell}</td>)}</tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<section class="section"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">MEASURED / TRANSPORT</p><h2>Four rates. All longer than a minute.</h2></div><p>The 2.048 MS/s gap is visible in the per-event log, even though the final integer-per-million figure rounded to zero.</p></div><RtlContinuity /><div class="table-scroll measurement-table"><table class="lab-table"><thead><tr><th>Configured rate</th><th>Streaming before SIGINT</th><th>Loss reports</th><th>Missing bytes, lower bound</th></tr></thead><tbody>{capture.runs.map(run => <tr><th scope="row">{run.requested_rate_hz/1e6} MS/s</th><td>{run.observed_stream_before_sigint_s.toFixed(3)} s</td><td>{run.loss_reports}</td><td>{run.reported_lost_bytes_lower_bound}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p class="calc-note">One trial per rate, normal cleanup, no controlled host-load sweep. Eight-bit counter wrapping can conceal gaps; recurring interval estimates reflect host/USB timing and do not calibrate the TCXO.</p></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">MEASURED / ESP SNAPSHOT TRANSPORT</p><h2>Six series. 600 validated payloads.</h2></div><p>Short nominal listening windows followed by roughly 361–451 ms command-to-payload cycles. CRC success does not identify the captured signal.</p></div><SnapshotTiming /></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">MEASURED / ESP SPECTRUM TRANSPORT</p><h2>The browser works. Reception is discontinuous.</h2></div><p>A 60-second 512-bin session passes sequence, CRC and end-total checks. Every frame flags a capture gap; no controlled source is identified.</p></div><BrowserSession /></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">MEASURED / RECEIVE-ONLY</p><h2>Signal structure, with its limits attached.</h2></div><p>A five-second normal-IQ capture around 101.1 MHz reproduces a 19 kHz feature after FM demodulation. This is consistent with a stereo pilot, not station or decoder proof.</p></div><a class="measurement-preview" href={evidenceUrl("docs/evidence/rtl-fm-survey/README.md")}><img src={evidenceAsset("docs/evidence/rtl-fm-survey/fm-structure.png")} alt="Actual measured FM candidate spectrum and spectrogram; station and antenna unverified" loading="lazy" /><span>Open original settings, sample-file hash, analysis and limitations ↗</span></a></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">APPLICATION MATRIX / PARTIAL</p><h2>Choose a receiver and a proof gate.</h2></div><p>Local observations, architectural expectations and unperformed application tests are distinct. ESP transfer timing is now measured. Controlled RF response, known-source applications and shared-signal sensitivity remain open.</p></div><div class="table-scroll"><table class="lab-table"><thead><tr><th>Application</th><th>Candidate</th><th>Evidence and next gate</th></tr></thead><tbody>{applications.map(row => <tr>{row.map((cell,index) => index===0 ? <th scope="row">{cell}</th> : <td>{cell}</td>)}</tr>)}</tbody></table></div></section>
<section class="section split"><article class="note-box"><h3>Shared-signal sensitivity is still open</h3><p>The stock useful bands do not overlap. Comparing sensitivity needs a common calibrated signal path, a characterized converter or documented reference sources, conversion loss and uncertainty. That physical inventory is unresolved.</p><p>A receiver’s output bit count alone cannot rank its sensitivity or dynamic range.</p><a href={url("work/?work=the-two-receivers-have-a-measured-division-of-labor")}>Open the remaining comparison gates →</a></article><article class="note-box"><h3>Current practical direction</h3><p>Develop continuous narrowband applications with the V4 and establish each selected antenna/decoder test. Use the ESP32 as an experimental 2.4 GHz snapshot candidate with measured transfer gaps and nominal time coverage, then verify controlled RF response.</p><p>Keep FPGA work bounded by measured data availability and transport capacity. The measured transport envelope supports these practical choices; same-signal sensitivity, known-source applications and FPGA integration remain open.</p><a href={url("fpga/")}>Review FPGA capacity limits →</a></article></section>
<section class="section prose-note"><p><a href={evidenceUrl("docs/research/measured-recommendations.md")}>Read the measured recommendations and full application matrix ↗</a></p><p>Primary references: <a href="https://www.rtl-sdr.com/rtl-sdr-blog-v4-dongle-initial-release/">V4 manufacturer design</a>, <a href="https://www.rtl-sdr.com/about-rtl-sdr/">RTL sampling and applications</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ESPARGOS/esp-sdr/tree/550fadea4d00a9e26ce921c5832167becb3dc20c">pinned ESP-SDR firmware</a> and <a href="https://www.itu.int/rec/R-REC-BS.450/en">FM pilot-tone system</a>.</p></section>
</Base>
